  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Difluprednate is a potent glucocorticoid used to treat eye disease and, as a skin preparation, inflammatory skin conditions. It is an approved medicine, available in ophthalmological and dermatological formulations, though not authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q736113\">Wikidata Q736113</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>difluprednate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>D07AC19, S01BA16</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=\"https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB06781\">DB06781</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=\"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/443936\">443936</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:31485\">31485</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q736113\">Q736113</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C27H34F2O7</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>508.558 g/mol (PubChem CID 443936)</td></tr><tr><td>logP:</td><td>3.4 (Drugs.Common 25.09, not verified)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
